{"availability":"available","full":"LopezGroup-ICIQ/ATLAS","name":"ATLAS","description":"An automatic workflow for streamlining training and data generation for MLIPs via active learning","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":8,"forks":2,"created":"2023-05-05T14:26:30Z","updated":"2026-09-15T07:30:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://lopezgroup-iciq.github.io/ATLAS/","topics":["active-learning","catalysis","chemistry","machine-learning","mlip"],"demo":"https://lopezgroup-iciq.github.io/ATLAS/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.434Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.434Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.434Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.434Z","stars":8,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Under Development: This library is still under active development and may contain bugs or undergo breaking changes. Use with caution in production or critical research workflows. Please report any bugs or issues using the Issues tab.","ATLAS (Automated Training with Latent-space Aware Sampling) is a unified Python framework for building robust machine learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs). It combines a diversity-aware database generator with a manifold-aware active learning workflow to produce compact, high-quality training datasets. Its latent-space awareness enables applicability checking during application. ATLAS supports structure generation for bulk, surface, cluster, and isolated atom configurations across single-, binary-, and ternary (WIP) phase diagrams, as well as user-defined element space, with perturbations,…","The active learning engine uses a modular backend architecture for MLIPs. It currently supports a growing list of models: MACE, Allegro, and NequIP for training, plus the pretrained foundation potentials Orb, fairchem (UMA/eSEN), and EquiformerV3 for inference (MD sampling and benchmarking). Any model can be added through the generic backend plugin interface. It runs molecular dynamics simulations, detects extrapolating structures via descriptor-based latent-space methods (autoencoder + concave hull or morphological shape), and submits them for DFT labelling, all orchestrated through AiiDA."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LopezGroup-ICIQ/ATLAS/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"3365ebe7ea14a6d09d406f95f0a120019d228462fa212719d35de1ba095a7675","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.580Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.580Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Under Development: This library is still under active development and may contain bugs or undergo breaking changes. Use with caution in production or critical research workflows. Please report any bugs or issues using the Issues tab.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LopezGroup-ICIQ/ATLAS/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3365ebe7ea14a6d09d406f95f0a120019d228462fa212719d35de1ba095a7675","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LopezGroup-ICIQ/ATLAS/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.580Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-15T07:30:00Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LopezGroup-ICIQ/ATLAS/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:13.581Z","hash":"3365ebe7ea14a6d09d406f95f0a120019d228462fa212719d35de1ba095a7675","originalBytes":19999,"storedBytes":19999,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["file","atlas","atl","configuration","learning","active","database","run","python","bash","environment","gui","gen","loop","mace","using","generate","install","model","path","training","activate","aiida","dft","initial","installation","create","generation","type","venv","which","available","conda","development","optional","pip","toml","any","commit","dependencies","documentation","example","fairchem","following","init","mlip","potentials","pre-commit","several","after","allegro","command","commit